new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e862b7e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PRIVACY_AUDIT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+# Privacy audit
+
+Scope: sign-in, sign-up, shared layout resources, response headers, and the
+reading-list initialization performed by shared middleware.
+
+## Changes
+
+- Account forms still collect only username and password. Inline notices identify
+  the external account-service host and purpose before submission, explain
+  connection metadata, and link to the updated privacy policy. Sign-up explicitly
+  supports a pseudonym; it does not add identity or marketing fields.
+- Credential requests remain HTTPS JSON POSTs, omit cookies and referrers, bypass
+  browser caching, and reject redirects to avoid forwarding credentials to a new
+  destination. Credentials and tokens are never written to browser storage.
+- Passwords clear after successful and unsuccessful attempts. Raw service errors
+  and response tokens are no longer parsed or surfaced. Password-manager autofill
+  uses username, current-password, and new-password semantics.
+- Forms declare POST even before hydration, preventing credentials from becoming
+  URL query parameters. The existing account integration requires JavaScript and
+  does not supply a server-rendered submission fallback.
+- Removed the global analytics loader and unused commented ad loader. Removed
+  Google Fonts and preconnections; the brand font uses a local system serif stack.
+  Ad slots remain inert placeholders with no external ad script loaded.
+- Middleware sets Referrer-Policy: no-referrer, Permissions-Policy denying unused
+  sensors and powerful features, and X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff. A head meta
+  referrer policy provides a document-level fallback. Account documents and
+  reading-list responses use Cache-Control: no-store.
+- Removed eager reading-list initialization on every request. The existing
+  reading-list POST is responsible for creating stored state after a save action.
+- Replaced generic privacy copy with descriptions of actual application behavior
+  and changed the nonfunctional privacy-preferences link to the relevant policy
+  section.
+
+## Boundaries and follow-up
+
+- The external account API implementation is outside this repository. Its password
+  hashing, account retention, logs, rate limits, and account export/deletion
+  procedures remain unverified. The privacy policy discloses these limitations
+  rather than promising retention or deletion behavior the app cannot enforce.
+- Existing externally hosted article images still disclose connection metadata to
+  their hosts. Hosting logs and the article-specific DevTools demonstration cookies
+  are disclosed; those demonstrations are outside this change's scope.
+- A complete script CSP/Trusted Types rollout needs separate framework and inline
+  script work. No broad script restrictions, reporting collection endpoints, or
+  cross-origin isolation policies were added without compatibility verification.
+- The existing service only reports sign-in success here; this change does not
+  introduce an authenticated session or persist returned tokens.
+
+## Validation
+
+`pnpm run build` and `git diff --check` passed. The build reported existing
+React/Vite deprecation warnings and ignored `getStaticPaths` declarations on the
+server-rendered article/category routes. No development/preview server, browser
+verification, server entrypoint imports, live credential requests, or production
+deployment were used for this audit.
