-    <h2>1. An overview of data protection</h2>
-    <p><strong>General information</strong></p>
-    <p>The following information will provide you with an easy to navigate overview of what will happen with your personal data when you visit our website. The term “personal data” comprises all data that can be used to personally identify you. For detailed information about the subject matter of data protection, please consult our Data Protection Declaration, which we have included beneath this copy.</p>
-    
-    <h2>2. General information and mandatory information</h2>
-    <p><strong>Data protection</strong></p>
-    <p>The operators of this website and its pages take the protection of your personal data very seriously. Hence, we handle your personal data as confidential information and in compliance with the statutory data protection regulations and this Data Protection Declaration.</p>
-    <p>Whenever you use this website, a variety of personal information will be collected. Personal data comprises data that can be used to personally identify you. This Data Protection Declaration explains which data we collect as well as the purposes we use this data for. It also explains how, and for which purpose the information is collected.</p>
-    
-    <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
-    <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
-    <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+    <h2>Account information</h2>
+    <p>You can read articles without creating an account. Sign-up asks only for a username and password. A pseudonym is enough; we do not ask for your real name, email address, date of birth, or phone number.</p>
+    <p>When you submit either account form, your browser sends your username and password over HTTPS to the external account service at <code class="break-all">us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net/times_cdn/api/</code> (register or login). The purpose is to create your account or check your credentials. The service also receives connection information, including your IP address. The forms do not send browsing history or additional profile fields, and do not include cookies in these requests.</p>
+    <p>The page keeps entered credentials in memory while you use the form and clears the password after each completed attempt. It does not write credentials or authentication tokens to localStorage, sessionStorage, or cookies. A password manager may separately offer to save your credentials under your browser settings.</p>
+
+    <h2>Analytics, advertising, and external resources</h2>
+    <p>The shared page layout does not load third-party analytics, advertising scripts, or remote fonts. Account form activity is not sent to analytics. No optional tracking is enabled, so you do not need to dismiss a consent banner to read the site.</p>
+    <p>Some articles and homepage content still use externally hosted images. Those hosts receive connection information when your browser requests an image. The site uses a no-referrer policy to keep the referring page URL out of those requests. Visiting an external link also connects you to that site's own services.</p>
+
+    <h2>Reading lists and demonstration data</h2>
+    <p>Reading-list storage begins when you explicitly save an article, rather than on every visit. Where sessions are available, the reading-list feature stores article identifiers and uses a session identifier to retrieve your list. You can remove articles using the same bookmark controls.</p>
+    <p>This is a Chrome DevTools demonstration site. Some article demonstrations set test cookies or call sample APIs. You can remove site cookies and storage through your browser's site-data settings; this also removes your browser's access to any saved reading list. It does not delete an account held by the external account service.</p>
+
+    <h2 id="privacy-choices">Privacy and data choices</h2>
+    <p>You can browse without an account and choose a pseudonym if you register. Only submit information you want to send to the account service. Clearing the form or leaving the page before submitting does not send your credentials to that service.</p>
+    <p>The source code for this site does not define the external account service's retention period, password-storage practices, or access, correction, and deletion procedures. Those practices have not been verified here. This site currently has no account deletion or data export interface. The hosting providers may also keep operational logs; their retention is not configured by this application.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
